
### restack rebases a branch checked out in another worktree, from there
$ git stack restack
restacking stack rooted at feat-a
restacking feat-b onto feat-a in worktree '<repo>-wt'
restacking feat-c onto feat-b
done.
[exit 0]
feat-b behind feat-a: 0
feat-c behind feat-b: 0
worktree HEAD: feat-b
worktree status: 0
HEAD: feat-a

### restack fast-forwards a branch with no commits in another worktree
$ git stack restack
restacking stack rooted at feat-a
fast-forwarding feat-b to feat-a in worktree '<repo>-wt'
done.
[exit 0]
feat-b == feat-a: yes
worktree file a2.txt: a2

### restack skips a branch whose worktree is dirty, with its descendants
$ git stack restack
restacking stack rooted at feat-a
warning: skipping 'feat-b': its worktree '<repo>-wt' has uncommitted changes
warning: skipping 'feat-c': its parent 'feat-b' was skipped
restacking feat-x onto feat-a
error: restack skipped 2 branch(es): feat-b, feat-c
Deal with the branches warned about above, then re-run 'git stack restack'.
[exit 1]
feat-b behind feat-a: 1
feat-c behind feat-a: 1
feat-x behind feat-a: 0
worktree change kept: dirty
HEAD: feat-a

### an untracked file does not make a worktree dirty
$ git stack restack
restacking stack rooted at feat-a
restacking feat-b onto feat-a in worktree '<repo>-wt'
done.
[exit 0]
feat-b behind feat-a: 0

### a dirty worktree is no reason to skip a branch with nothing to move
$ git stack restack
restacking stack rooted at feat-a
done.
[exit 0]

### restack skips a branch whose worktree is mid-rebase (listed as detached)
worktree listed as: 1
$ git stack restack
restacking stack rooted at feat-a
warning: skipping 'feat-b': its worktree '<repo>-wt' has a rebase in progress
error: restack skipped 1 branch(es): feat-b
Deal with the branches warned about above, then re-run 'git stack restack'.
[exit 1]
worktree still rebasing: 1

### restack skips a branch whose worktree directory is gone
$ git stack restack
restacking stack rooted at feat-a
warning: skipping 'feat-b': its worktree '<repo>-wt' is missing (see 'git worktree prune')
error: restack skipped 1 branch(es): feat-b
Deal with the branches warned about above, then re-run 'git stack restack'.
[exit 1]

### a conflict in another worktree is aborted there, with a cd to resolve it
$ git stack restack
restacking stack rooted at feat-a
restacking feat-b onto feat-a in worktree '<repo>-wt'
error: conflict while rebasing 'feat-b' onto 'feat-a' in worktree '<repo>-wt'.
Resolve it manually with:
    cd '<repo>-wt' && git rebase feat-a
then re-run 'git stack restack'.
[exit 1]
worktree still rebasing: 0
worktree HEAD: feat-b
HEAD: feat-a

### sync heals an orphan checked out in another worktree
$ git stack sync
syncing stack rooted at main
syncing stack rooted at feat-b
'feat-b': parent 'feat-a' no longer exists; reparenting onto trunk 'main'
restacking feat-b onto main in worktree '<repo>-wt'
done.
[exit 0]
feat-b parent: main
feat-b commits above main: 1
worktree HEAD: feat-b

### drop restacks a child checked out in another worktree
$ git stack drop feat-a
dropped feat-a; reparented children onto main
restacking feat-b onto main in worktree '<repo>-wt'
[exit 0]
feat-b parent: main
feat-b behind main: 0
HEAD: main

### drop still splices when a moved child is skipped, then reports it
$ git stack drop --delete feat-a
dropped feat-a; reparented children onto main
warning: skipping 'feat-b': its worktree '<repo>-wt' has uncommitted changes
deleted branch feat-a
error: restack skipped 1 branch(es): feat-b
Deal with the branches warned about above, then re-run 'git stack restack'.
[exit 1]
feat-b parent: main
feat-a exists: no
